==English==
{{wikipedia|Firewall (networking)}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈfaɪə.wɔəl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈfaɪ.əˌwɔːl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈfaɪ(ə)rˌwɔl/|/ˈfaɪ(ə)rˌwɑl/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-firewall.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|fire|wall|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Firewall (construction)}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[fireproof]] [[barrier]] used to [[prevent]] the [[spread]] of [[fire]] between or through [[buildings]], structures, electrical [[substation]] transformers, or within an aircraft or vehicle.
# {{context|computer security|lang=en}} The [[software]] that [[monitor]]s [[traffic]] in and out of a [[private]] [[network]] or a [[personal computer]] and [[allow]]s or [[block]]s such traffic depending on its [[perceive]]d [[threat]].

====Derived terms====
* [[Great Firewall of China]]

